-- title:
--   Measurability into a restricted product is coordinatewise
-- statement:
--   Let $\iota$ be a countable index type and let $R_i$, $i \in \iota$, be topological spaces, each second countable and each equipped with a measurable space structure that is its Borel $\sigma$-algebra. Let $A_i \subseteq R_i$ be subsets, and assume each $A_i$ is measurable. Consider the restricted product $\Pi^{r}_{i}\,[R_i, A_i]$ taken with respect to the cofinite filter, i.e. the space of families $(y_i)_{i \in \iota}$ with $y_i \in A_i$ for all but finitely many $i$, with its restricted product topology, and assume it too carries a measurable space structure equal to its Borel $\sigma$-algebra. Then for every measurable space $X$ and every map $f \colon X \to \Pi^{r}_{i}\,[R_i, A_i]$, the map $f$ is measurable if and only if for each $i \in \iota$ the coordinate map $x \mapsto f(x)_i$ is a measurable map $X \to R_i$. Equivalently, the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of the restricted product is generated by the coordinate evaluations.
--
--   This identifies the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of a restricted product over a countable index set with the $\sigma$-algebra generated by the coordinates, the measure-theoretic counterpart of the usual description of the restricted product topology; it is the basic measurability criterion used when integrating over adelic groups. It is used in the construction of measurable functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles and in the associated integral identities over unipotent subgroups.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_RestrictedProduct_measurable_iff_forall_measurable_apply.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open MeasureTheory
open scoped RestrictedProduct

theorem RestrictedProduct.measurable_iff_forall_measurable_apply
    {ι : Type*} [Countable ι] {R : ι → Type*}
    [∀ i, TopologicalSpace (R i)] [∀ i, SecondCountableTopology (R i)]
    [∀ i, MeasurableSpace (R i)] [∀ i, BorelSpace (R i)]
    {A : (i : ι) → Set (R i)} (hA : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (A i))
    [MeasurableSpace (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])] [BorelSpace (Πʳ i, [R i, A i])]
    {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] (f : X → Πʳ i, [R i, A i]) :
    Measurable f ↔ ∀ i, Measurable fun x => f x i := by sorry
